    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "14",
      "answer": "τοὺς ἑαυτῶν νεανίσκους ‘their own young men’ (lit. the young men of themselves).\nἕπεσθαι Note the rough breathing. It is from ἔπομαι ‘I follow’.",
      "src": {
        "book": "guide",
        "printed_page": "96",
        "pdf_page": 110
      }
    },
    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "15",
      "answer": "εἴποντο What verb? What had they been told to do?",
      "src": {
        "book": "guide",
        "printed_page": "96",
        "pdf_page": 110
      }
    },
    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "16",
      "answer": "ἀπῆλθον ... ἀπελθοῦσαι The pattern as before.",
      "src": {
        "book": "guide",
        "printed_page": "96",
        "pdf_page": 110
      }
    },
    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "3",
      "answer": "εἰς τὸ αὐτὸ χωρίον ‘to the same place’, αὐτός preceded by the article always means ‘the same’. See GE pp. 153–155, #172–176 for the different uses of αὐτός. Be careful to distinguish between αὐτόν ‘him’ and ἑαυτόν (or αὐτόν) reflexive ‘himself’.",
      "src": {
        "book": "guide",
        "printed_page": "96",
        "pdf_page": 110
      }
    },
    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "4",
      "answer": "τὸ αὐτό ‘the same thing’.\nἄξξει What tense? What verb?",
      "src": {
        "book": "guide",
        "printed_page": "96",
        "pdf_page": 110
      }
    },
    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "5",
      "answer": "τῇ δ᾽ ὑστεραίᾳ ‘on the next day’. Dative of time when.\nαὐτός ‘himself’, emphatic; agrees with the subject: ‘coming himself ...’",
      "src": {
        "book": "guide",
        "printed_page": "96",
        "pdf_page": 110
      }
    },
    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "6",
      "answer": "τὴν Ἀμαζόνα αὐτήν ‘the Amazon herself’ (emphatic).",
      "src": {
        "book": "guide",
        "printed_page": "96",
        "pdf_page": 110
      }
    },
    {
      "exercise_id": "7H",
      "item": "8",
      "answer": "ἐποίουν τὸ αὐτὸ καὶ αὐτοί Cf. lines 4 and 5 ‘they did the same thing themselves also’.",
